From 47e257835ecc50461d23879dc06a2b8858d36eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:42:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 03/29] mrt: N-output typed emitter, executor validation, and
 the generic MRT pass runner

Frontier-92 2.2 diagnosed two frontend bugs blocking MRT (drawBuffers >= 2):
tools/glslcpp/emit_typed_cpp.py's name() resolved every declared output
symbol to the identical C++ identifier "output" (glsl::Vec4& output), so
only the last write survived; and frontend/preprocess.py's normalize()
regex only matched plain `out T name;`, silently under-detecting
`layout(location=N) out T name;` and returning ["fragColor"] for every
MRT program (papered over for storage="output" classification by
semantic.py's `"out" in quals` OR-branch, but not for the outputs list
itself, which feeds the pinned corpus manifest and generate_typed_slice's
ABI serialization).

Frontend (tools/glslcpp):
- preprocess.py: detect `layout(location=N) out vec4 name;`, appending to
  the outputs census in declaration order without rewriting the line (so
  no already-pinned single-output corpus entry's normalized bytes/hash can
  move). Assert N against the output's own ascending position -- the JS
  authority sorts its outputNames by location
  (scripts/upstream/compile-glsl.js), and every pinned upstream MRT source
  happens to declare locations in ascending source order today, but that
  was never asserted before.
- emit_typed_cpp.py: an arity/collision guard at typed-program construction
  (distinct emitted identifier per output, symbol-id-suffixed on a
  reserved-name collision, fail-closed on any duplicate); name() keeps
  returning the literal "output" for exactly one declared output (byte
  identity for every existing single-output program) and otherwise returns
  each output's own slot name; render_body emits an N-output
  `pixel(..., glsl::Vec4* outputs)` with per-output `Vec4&` aliases into
  `outputs[slot]`, and the factory returns BoundKernelMrt(state, &pixel, N)
  instead of BoundKernel. Guarded off for every existing single-output
  hand-authored capability (remap/median/mutable-frame/palette/testpattern/
  runtime-loop/fixed-array/derivatives) until proven in combination.

Runtime (kernel.hpp/.cpp, pass_runner.hpp/.cpp):
- BoundKernelMrt: the MRT sibling of BoundKernel, N persistent Vec4
  registers instead of one frag_color_ -- the direct analog of the JS
  authority's per-output Float32Array(4) closure variables
  (fragColor/geoOut/... allocated once per factory call, mutated in place
  every pixel, never per-call). Refuses <2 outputs and uses_derivatives
  (no admitted MRT program uses dFdx/dFdy/fwidth; there is no quad-replay
  wrapper for this constructor).
- run_mrt_pass: mirrors runCanonicalMrtPass's raster order and fragCoord
  convention exactly (renderer.js:450-490) -- one kernel call per pixel
  produces every output atomically, scattered into N Surfaces. Same
  "quantize off-route" convention as run_pass: raw float32 out, caller
  quantizes each Surface via the same quantize_texture.

Executor (src/graph/executor.cpp, include/.../executor.hpp):
- validate_pass_output_abi generalized from a hardcoded single-output
  check to walking every (pass.outputs[i], admission.outputs[i]) pair;
  the "physical_name" a single-output pass may alias to ("color" on 19
  rows) only applies at N==1 -- an MRT pass's declared key must already be
  the real GLSL symbol name, verified against every pinned upstream MRT
  source.
- Both `draw_buffers != 1.0` refusals (the plan dry-run loop and
  validate_pass_controls) now compare the declared drawBuffers count
  against the pass's own output count instead of hardcoding 1: an ordinary
  pass (draw_buffers absent, one output) is unaffected, and unsupported_mrt
  now means "declared count disagrees with actual output count," not
  "more than one output."
- FactoryRouteDescriptorMrt/find_factory_route_mrt/
  canonical_factory_routes_mrt/authenticate_factory_route_mrt/
  bind_factory_route_mrt: the MRT sibling of the existing route-authentication
  chain, reusing binding_abi_sections (already output-count-generic) for the
  ordered-ABI cross-check. canonical_factory_routes_mrt() is empty today --
  no MRT program has been compiled by the typed-slice generator yet -- so
  this refuses every lookup until that lands, exactly like
  bind_factory_route's routes-span override already lets a caller supply
  its own table.
- GraphExecutor::execute()'s real dispatch loop branches on
  admission.outputs.size(): the MRT branch resolves every declared output's
  own destination texture spec independently and asserts they share
  dimensions BEFORE binding a kernel (canonicalMrtDestinations/
  assertMrtDestinationsShareDimensions, renderer.js:519-533) -- run_mrt_pass
  itself doesn't re-check, mirroring runCanonicalMrtPass exactly -- then
  quantizes and inserts each destination independently, threading `current`
  through whichever output routes to "outputTex" (if any).

No currently-admitted effect has more than one output, so canonicalFactory
lookups for N>1 are unreachable in production today; this lands the
primitive and proves it, per the task's own scoping, ahead of the corpus
expansion that will actually admit Family D/E's MRT programs.

Proof:
- Byte-identical generated output: check_corpus --check and
  generate_typed_slice --check (211 typed programs) both pass with hashes
  unchanged from before this change.
- Differential against the JS authority: four synthetic programs (2/3/4
  outputs, one with a branch) compiled through the real typed pipeline
  (parse_program -> analyze_program -> render_typed_cpp) and through the
  authority's own compile-glsl.js pipeline pieces (normalizeCanonicalGlsl +
  glsl-transpiler + bindCanonicalKernel, run via Node against the read-only
  authority checkout, never regenerating its files), compared bit-exact
  across 9 sizes x 5 seeds: 343,200 float32 comparisons, 0 divergent.
- Native suite: 552/553 pass; the one failure
  (typed_classic_noise_oracle_metadata_is_complete_and_load_bearing) is
  confirmed pre-existing by rebuilding the pristine base commit in an
  isolated clone.
- DSL corpus parity lane (tests.test_dsl_corpus_parity): fails identically
  (162 != 155 byteExactCount) on both this branch and a pristine clone of
  the base commit -- pre-existing.
- Parity sweep (208 effects, 4685 variants) against a pristine clone's own
  208/4685 baseline sweep: byte_exact/divergent/both_refused identical
  (3212/89/15, same 30 divergent effects); refused+timeout sums identical
  (1369) with only the split shifted by shared-machine scheduling noise on
  two never-rendered, still-unadmitted effects (both refused with the
  ordinary "missing_backend_program" reason, unrelated to this change).
- Full Python suite: every pre-existing failure (63 in test_typed_generator
  alone; 42 more across 18 other historical-reconstruction/committed-artifact
  test modules) reproduced byte-for-byte identically on a pristine clone of
  the base commit.
- New: tests/test_mrt_kernel_and_pass_runner.cpp (9 cases) proves
  BoundKernelMrt/run_mrt_pass directly -- null/arity/derivative rejection,
  one-call-per-pixel atomicity, output[0] byte-identical to run_pass for an
  identical expression, cross-call register persistence, and quantization
  through the same API as the single-output path.

Blocked on: the corpus304 lane's corpus expansion (211/212 -> 304 programs)
landing real Family D/E MRT sources; end-to-end admission proof on those
real programs is explicitly deferred to that merge, per the task brief.

